# App UI non-negotiables

These are the always-on rules. For the full how-to (spacing scale, typography, icons), the **`app-ui` skill** carries the detail — activate it whenever you build or restyle UI.

## Vuetify-first

- Always reach for a Vuetify component (`v-btn`, `v-card`, `v-dialog`, `v-text-field`, etc.) before hand-rolling markup.
- Use `vuetify-inertia-link` / `to` props for in-app navigation inside Vuetify components.
- Compose with Vouch surface classes (`surface-raised`, `surface-chrome-*`) and token utilities.
- Build bespoke markup only when no Vuetify primitive fits.

## Design tokens, never raw color

- Never hardcode hex/rgb/oklch in components. Use semantic tokens: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-muted`, `text-destructive`, etc.
- The token registry is `resources/css/tokens/` (`shadcn-vars.css`, `tokens.css`). Brand intent lives in `.ai/design/brand.md`.
- Vuetify theme colors bridge from CSS vars via `resources/js/theme/tokens.ts`.

## Reuse before creating

- Check `resources/js/pages`, `resources/js/components`, and sibling feature files for an existing pattern before writing a new one.
- Use full shell/layout composition — see **`DemoA.vue`** / **`DemoB.vue`** and `layouts/app.vue`.

## Icons

- Use Iconify with Lucide collection: `<v-icon icon="lucide:..." />` or `IconifyIcon`.
